      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per in-person discussion, if we make this a build method that\u0027s used by the recipient of the parcel, then if we want to send a new type of keepalive packet, then the ensure that the recipient of the parcel must has the knowledge of all the information necessary to generate the full header.\n\nThat means we\u0027ll need to modify this class to store such new information and that the recipient will need access to any information that is necessary to construct the packet. ISTM that that is a reduction in functionality compared to having the network stack construct the whole packet and passing it around.\n\nGiven that we\u0027ll need to pass around the payload anyway it seems like we could continue to pass around the whole packet.",
